\pard\hyphpar0\sb15\sa15\fi0\li0\ri0\ql\fs18{\f0 Treatment groups are PLANNED treatment (TRT01P). Twelve subjects in this study received a treatment other than the one they were randomised to; grouping by actual treatment (TRT01A) would give column sizes of 86, 96 and 72.\line A subject is counted once per therapeutic class and once per coded medication, however many records they have. Class counts are therefore not the sum of the medication counts beneath them.\line Every recorded medication counts, whether it was taken before, during or after treatment. Restricting to medications taken on treatment (ONTRTFL = 'Y') would count a much smaller set of records.\line UNCODED is not a therapeutic class. It is how this study's data records a medication that was never coded to a dictionary term, and it is reported rather than dropped.\line Classes, and the medications within a class, are ordered by the largest subject count in any treatment group, ties alphabetically. The reference document this display targets ordered them alphabetically by class instead.\line Percentages are based on the number of subjects in the safety analysis set for each treatment group.}\cell
